insert into questions (id, certification_id, prompt, theory, topic, difficulty, position, published) values
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000501','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','A value is defined in application.yml and also supplied through an environment variable. Which source normally takes precedence in Spring Boot?','External environment variables have higher precedence than values packaged in application.yml, which makes deployment configuration possible without rebuilding the application.','Configuration','Level 2',11,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000502','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','What should be added to a controller method parameter to trigger Bean Validation annotations such as @NotBlank on a request DTO?','@Valid tells Spring MVC to validate the request object using its Bean Validation constraints before the controller method continues.','Validation','Level 2',12,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000503','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Where is cross-cutting HTTP exception handling commonly placed in a Spring Boot REST API?','@RestControllerAdvice centralises exception-to-response mapping for REST controllers.','Error handling','Level 2',13,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000504','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Which annotation is commonly used on a service method that performs several database changes which must succeed or fail together?','@Transactional creates a transaction boundary so the related database work can be committed or rolled back together.','Data access','Level 2',14,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000505','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','For a group of related settings such as payment.gateway.url and payment.gateway.timeout, which approach gives type-safe configuration binding?','@ConfigurationProperties binds a related configuration prefix into a typed object and is preferable to many scattered @Value fields.','Configuration','Level 2',15,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000506','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','A REST endpoint creates a new resource. Which response is most appropriate when it succeeds?','HTTP 201 Created communicates that a new resource was successfully created.','REST APIs','Level 2',16,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000507','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Which Spring Boot feature exposes production-ready endpoints such as health and metrics?','Spring Boot Actuator provides operational endpoints such as /actuator/health and metrics.','Operations','Level 2',17,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000508','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','What does @Cacheable do when the same method is called again with the same cache key?','@Cacheable returns the cached result when available instead of executing the method again.','Performance','Level 2',18,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000509','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','What must be enabled for methods annotated with @Async to run through Spring asynchronous execution?','@EnableAsync enables Spring''s asynchronous method execution support.','Concurrency','Level 2',19,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000510','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Two implementations of the same interface are Spring beans. What is a clean way to select the intended implementation at an injection point?','@Qualifier selects a specific bean when multiple beans of the same type exist.','Dependency injection','Level 2',20,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000511','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','A @Transactional method calls another @Transactional method on the same object using this.otherMethod(). Why might the inner transaction settings not apply?','Spring transactions are usually applied by a proxy. A self-invocation does not pass through that proxy, so the inner method interception is skipped.','Transactions','Level 3',21,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000512','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','A controller returns a JPA entity and later accessing a lazy relationship throws LazyInitializationException. What is the best API design response?','Map the data to a DTO inside the service transaction and fetch the required relationships intentionally, instead of exposing entities directly from the controller.','JPA','Level 3',22,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000513','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Loading 50 orders and then reading customer.getName() for each causes many extra queries. What problem is this?','This is the N+1 query problem. A fetch join, entity graph or suitable projection can load the needed relationship efficiently.','JPA','Level 3',23,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000514','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','A method marked with propagation REQUIRES_NEW is called through the Spring proxy while another transaction is active. What happens?','REQUIRES_NEW suspends the existing transaction and starts an independent transaction for the inner operation.','Transactions','Level 3',24,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000515','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','By default, which exception type causes a Spring @Transactional method to roll back?','Spring rolls back by default for unchecked exceptions such as RuntimeException and Error. Checked exceptions require explicit rollback configuration when needed.','Transactions','Level 3',25,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000516','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','In modern Spring Security configuration, where are authorization rules commonly defined?','A SecurityFilterChain bean is the standard place to configure authorization, authentication and CSRF behaviour.','Security','Level 3',26,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000517','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Two users edit the same record. Which JPA feature helps detect the conflicting update instead of silently overwriting data?','A field annotated with @Version enables optimistic locking and detects conflicting updates.','Data integrity','Level 3',27,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000518','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Spring fails to start because ServiceA needs ServiceB and ServiceB needs ServiceA through constructor injection. What is the preferred fix?','Refactor the responsibilities to remove the circular dependency. Constructor injection makes the design issue visible early.','Architecture','Level 3',28,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000519','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','Which environment variable name maps naturally to the Spring Boot property server.port?','Spring Boot relaxed binding maps SERVER_PORT to server.port.','Configuration','Level 3',29,true),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000520','10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','A request body fails validation. Which HTTP status should a well-designed REST API normally return?','A validation failure is normally a client error, so Spring applications commonly return HTTP 400 Bad Request with useful field details.','Validation','Level 3',30,true);
